        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0262" n="166" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.115 St 21/427</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Unofficial Representative on the Reparation
                        Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hill</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 24.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my telegram H–124, of July 20,
                        1926,<anchor n="11" xml:id="d113-f1"/> I beg to enclose herewith five copies
                    of the English translation of the decision of Messrs. Sjoeborg and Lyon (Amiex
                    2953b) and five copies of the dissenting opinion of Colonel Bayne (Annex 2953c)
                    in the D. A. P. G. Tanker case. I am also enclosing five copies of the
                    transmitting letter.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d113-f2"/></p>
                <p>The decision of Messrs. Sjoeborg and Lyon was rendered in French and the
                    translation was only received today in time to go in the pouch. I have not yet
                    had an opportunity therefore to study it.</p>
                <p>I am sending, two copies of the English text of the decisions to Mr. Piesse, the
                    Counsel of the Standard Oil Company in New York.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ralph W. S. Hill</hi></signed></closer>




